From: EasyStick maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] esp32_sdio: name WQ_PERCPU explicitly in alloc_workqueue

Linux 7.x WARN_ONCE()s when alloc_workqueue() gets neither WQ_PERCPU
nor WQ_UNBOUND (workqueue is migrating to unbound-by-default).
flags=0 meant the legacy bound per-CPU pool, so spell WQ_PERCPU to
keep identical behaviour on 6.18 and 7.x.  The create_*() and
alloc_ordered_workqueue() helpers already OR in WQ_UNBOUND and need
no change.

---
diff --git a/main.c b/main.c
index 8fb6d3d..75664a1 100644
--- a/main.c
+++ b/main.c
@@ -1049,7 +1049,7 @@
 	memset(&adapter, 0, sizeof(adapter));
 
 	/* Prepare interface RX work */
-	adapter.if_rx_workqueue = alloc_workqueue("ESP_IF_RX_WORK_QUEUE", 0, 0);
+	adapter.if_rx_workqueue = alloc_workqueue("ESP_IF_RX_WORK_QUEUE", WQ_PERCPU, 0);
 
 	if (!adapter.if_rx_workqueue) {
 		deinit_adapter();
@@ -1060,7 +1060,7 @@
 
 	skb_queue_head_init(&adapter.events_skb_q);
 
-	adapter.events_wq = alloc_workqueue("ESP_EVENTS_WORKQUEUE", WQ_HIGHPRI, 0);
+	adapter.events_wq = alloc_workqueue("ESP_EVENTS_WORKQUEUE", WQ_HIGHPRI | WQ_PERCPU, 0);
 
 	if (!adapter.events_wq) {
 		deinit_adapter();
